# Naming conventions

Method and type names should encode **layer role** (decide / transmit / serialize) and **outcome**, not “we might do something.” Prefer Dragonfly-style `try*` / Zenith `Try*` for fallible ops; never invent a parallel `Maybe*` dialect.

Full table + examples: [`docs/naming.md`](../../docs/naming.md).

## Verb prefixes (required)

| Prefix | Returns | Meaning | Typical home |
|--------|---------|---------|----------------|
| `Handle*` | void | Inbound packet → validate → `Submit*` | `Session/Handler` |
| `Submit*` / `TryConsume*` | void / bool | Intent queue write / drain | `Player/` |
| `Apply*` | void / bool | System applies an intent (mutates if gates pass) | `Gameplay/Systems` |
| `Try*` | bool | Expected failure without throw | any |
| `Is*` / `Can*` | bool | Predicate only (no mutation) | any |
| `Send*` | void | Build + transmit packet | `Protocol/` |
| `Relay*` / `Announce*` | void | Peer orchestration | `Session/` helpers |
| `*Fanout` | void | Multi-peer FX (crack, lid, sound) | `Gameplay/` |
| `Begin*` / `Abort*` / `Complete*` / `Mark*` | void | Lifecycle state | `Player/` + systems |

## Conditional tick work (no `Maybe*`)

Name **outcome + condition**:

```csharp
// ❌ MaybeAbortIdleDig / MaybeUpdateDigTool
// ✅
AbortIdleDigIfStale(...)
UpdateDigToolIfHeldChanged(...)
```

Early-return inside is fine; the name must still say what happens when the condition holds.

## Banned / discouraged

| Avoid | Why |
|-------|-----|
| `Maybe*` | Ambiguous; use `If*` / `Try*` / outcome+condition |
| `Do*` / `Process*` / `Check*` that mutates | Vague; say Apply / Abort / Mark |
| `Send*` outside `Protocol/` | Handlers/Systems call Protocol; they do not encode |
| Gameplay referencing `DataPacket` / `BinaryStream` | Layering, not naming — still a blocker |

## Quick examples

- Handler: `HandleAuthInput` → `player.SubmitDigStart`
- System: `ApplyDig`, `ApplyEdit`, `AbortIdleDigIfStale`
- Protocol: `SendMoveAbsolute`, `SendLevelSoundEvent`
- Fan-out: `BlockCrackFanout.Start`, `BlockSoundFanout.Place`
- Visibility: `AnnounceJoin`, `RelaySkin`, `RefreshPeerView`
